steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1780047594
      nanos: 176764664
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Here is the master setup for Google AI Studio. Since you are building a responsive web app and are under a strict 1-hour time limit, we will split this into the System Instruction (the intelligence you configure in the AI Studio UI) and the UI Generation Prompt (what you will ask the model to code for you).\n\n1. The AI Studio System Instruction (The Brain)\nPaste this exactly into the \"System Instructions\" box in Google AI Studio. Set the model to Gemma 4, enable JSON mode if available, and keep the temperature low (around 0.2) for reliable formatting.\n\nYou are a dual-purpose mental health AI system. Your role is to empathetically respond to patients in distress while simultaneously generating clinical triage data for medical professionals.\n\nYou will receive raw input from a patient (either text or transcribed audio).\n\nYou must output a strictly formatted JSON object and nothing else. Do not use markdown blocks, just the raw JSON. The JSON must follow this exact schema:\n\n{\n\"patient_response\": \"A short, empathetic, non-clinical response spoken directly to the patient to validate their feelings and offer a micro-intervention.\",\n\"clinician_summary\": {\n\"primary_stressor\": \"1-3 word summary of the main issue\",\n\"risk_level\": \"Low, Medium, or High\",\n\"clinical_notes\": \"A brief, professional clinical observation of the patient\'s state.\",\n\"transcript\": \"A verbatim transcript of what the patient said.\"\n},\n\"crisis_trigger\": boolean\n}\n\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: You must set crisis_trigger to true ONLY if the patient expresses a clear, immediate intent for self-harm, suicide, or physical danger. Otherwise, it must be false.\n\n2. The Web UI Generation Prompt (The Frontend)\nPaste this into AI Studio (or your IDE) to generate the single-page application (SPA) boilerplate using vanilla HTML, JavaScript, and Tailwind CSS. This guarantees it works instantly without a complex build pipeline.\n\nWrite a single-page responsive web application using HTML, vanilla JavaScript, and Tailwind CSS (via CDN). The app is a two-sided mental health platform with a mobile-first design.\n\nArchitecture Overview:\nInclude a simple toggle at the very top of the page to switch between \"Patient View\" and \"Clinician View\".\n\nPatient View (Mobile-First, Calming Vibe):\n\nDesign a minimalist, soft-blue and warm-white interface.\n\nCenter a large, prominent \"Record Voice Journal\" button.\n\nInclude a text box below it labeled \"Or type your journal here...\" and a \"Submit to Gemma\" button.\n\nCrisis Modal (Hidden by default): Create a full-screen, high-contrast dark overlay. It should say \"Your safety is our priority.\" Include two massive, unmistakable red buttons: one linking to tel:14416 (Tele MANAS) and one to tel:112 (National Emergency).\n\nLogic: When the user clicks \"Submit\", simulate an API call that returns a JSON object. If the JSON has \"crisis_trigger\": true, instantly show the Crisis Modal and lock the rest of the screen. If false, display the patient_response in a soft text bubble.\n\nClinician View (Responsive Dashboard, Clinical Vibe):\n\nDesign a clean, structured grid layout.\n\nCreate a JavaScript function that takes the JSON response and renders it into a \"Patient Card\".\n\nThe card must display the primary_stressor, risk_level, clinical_notes, and transcript.\n\nRed Alert Logic: If \"crisis_trigger\": true, the card\'s background must turn a warning red, and a \"Requires Immediate Escalation\" banner must appear at the top of the card.\n\nOutput the complete, runnable code in a single index.html file so I can open it directly in my browser and start pitching."
    items {
      text: "Here is the master setup for Google AI Studio. Since you are building a responsive web app and are under a strict 1-hour time limit, we will split this into the System Instruction (the intelligence you configure in the AI Studio UI) and the UI Generation Prompt (what you will ask the model to code for you).\n\n1. The AI Studio System Instruction (The Brain)\nPaste this exactly into the \"System Instructions\" box in Google AI Studio. Set the model to Gemma 4, enable JSON mode if available, and keep the temperature low (around 0.2) for reliable formatting.\n\nYou are a dual-purpose mental health AI system. Your role is to empathetically respond to patients in distress while simultaneously generating clinical triage data for medical professionals.\n\nYou will receive raw input from a patient (either text or transcribed audio).\n\nYou must output a strictly formatted JSON object and nothing else. Do not use markdown blocks, just the raw JSON. The JSON must follow this exact schema:\n\n{\n\"patient_response\": \"A short, empathetic, non-clinical response spoken directly to the patient to validate their feelings and offer a micro-intervention.\",\n\"clinician_summary\": {\n\"primary_stressor\": \"1-3 word summary of the main issue\",\n\"risk_level\": \"Low, Medium, or High\",\n\"clinical_notes\": \"A brief, professional clinical observation of the patient\'s state.\",\n\"transcript\": \"A verbatim transcript of what the patient said.\"\n},\n\"crisis_trigger\": boolean\n}\n\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION: You must set crisis_trigger to true ONLY if the patient expresses a clear, immediate intent for self-harm, suicide, or physical danger. Otherwise, it must be false.\n\n2. The Web UI Generation Prompt (The Frontend)\nPaste this into AI Studio (or your IDE) to generate the single-page application (SPA) boilerplate using vanilla HTML, JavaScript, and Tailwind CSS. This guarantees it works instantly without a complex build pipeline.\n\nWrite a single-page responsive web application using HTML, vanilla JavaScript, and Tailwind CSS (via CDN). The app is a two-sided mental health platform with a mobile-first design.\n\nArchitecture Overview:\nInclude a simple toggle at the very top of the page to switch between \"Patient View\" and \"Clinician View\".\n\nPatient View (Mobile-First, Calming Vibe):\n\nDesign a minimalist, soft-blue and warm-white interface.\n\nCenter a large, prominent \"Record Voice Journal\" button.\n\nInclude a text box below it labeled \"Or type your journal here...\" and a \"Submit to Gemma\" button.\n\nCrisis Modal (Hidden by default): Create a full-screen, high-contrast dark overlay. It should say \"Your safety is our priority.\" Include two massive, unmistakable red buttons: one linking to tel:14416 (Tele MANAS) and one to tel:112 (National Emergency).\n\nLogic: When the user clicks \"Submit\", simulate an API call that returns a JSON object. If the JSON has \"crisis_trigger\": true, instantly show the Crisis Modal and lock the rest of the screen. If false, display the patient_response in a soft text bubble.\n\nClinician View (Responsive Dashboard, Clinical Vibe):\n\nDesign a clean, structured grid layout.\n\nCreate a JavaScript function that takes the JSON response and renders it into a \"Patient Card\".\n\nThe card must display the primary_stressor, risk_level, clinical_notes, and transcript.\n\nRed Alert Logic: If \"crisis_trigger\": true, the card\'s background must turn a warning red, and a \"Requires Immediate Escalation\" banner must appear at the top of the card.\n\nOutput the complete, runnable code in a single index.html file so I can open it directly in my browser and start pitching."
    }
  }
}
