  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Frontend**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the frontend within `/src/App.tsx`. The initial plan is to build a toggle for \"Patient View\" and \"Clinician View,\" which will be positioned prominently at the top. I\'m aiming for a calming and elegant aesthetic.\n\n\n**Refining the Interface**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the \"Mood First\" design principles. I\'ve selected a calming color palette with soft-blues and warm-whites, including shades like `bg-[#f8fafc]` and `bg-[#f0f4f8]` paired with crisp white cards. The typography is clean and uses a default premium combination. I\'m also planning responsive container max widths and custom audio record indicators with pulse animations. For the \"Patient View,\" I\'m centering the experience around a prominent \"Record Voice Journal\" button that triggers a browser-standard voice recording. I\'m ensuring graceful handling of mic permission issues, and planning a full mic capture flow and visualizer for professional use.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Engagement**\n\nI\'m now integrating dynamic visual feedback during voice recording. I\'ll implement a ticking timer and a responsive SVG audio waveform, driven by real-time microphone input using Web Audio API\'s `AudioContext` and `AnalyserNode`. Below this, I\'m adding a text box alternative for text-based journaling. On submission, I\'ll display a loading skeleton and then render a full-screen crisis modal if the analysis detects a crisis trigger. The crisis modal is designed with high contrast, prominently featuring emergency contacts and a \"Close Safety Warning\" button.\n\n\n**Developing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the clinician view, envisioning a responsive grid dashboard. Each assessment card will display summaries, stressors, notes, and transcripts, with risk levels visually indicated by color-coded badges, ranging from blue/green (low) to glowing red (crisis). I\'ll fetch patient data using `/api/triage-history`, perhaps with a refresh button. Crisis cards will have red backgrounds and a prominent alert banner. I\'ll include \"Acknowledge Alert\" and \"Mark as Resolved\" buttons to manage crisis escalations, plus some filters and a search bar for easy navigation. I\'ll also show a clear status card if the Gemini API key is missing.\n\n\n"
