  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing App Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing `/src/App.tsx`. I\'ve begun to design the key sections, including state management. I\'m considering `activeTab`, which can be either `\'patient\'` or `\'clinician\'`, the `triageHistory` fetched from `/api/triage-history`, and `journalText`. I want the app to be beautiful, so I\'m paying special attention to the visual flow of these components.\n\n\n**Refining Audio Recording**\n\nI\'m now integrating comprehensive audio recording features. I am defining and integrating state variables for managing audio states, including `isRecording`, `recordingSeconds`, `micError`, and `micVolume`. I\'m also implementing the `startRecording` function, which leverages `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia` to access the microphone and handle potential errors. I\'m also setting up `mediaRecorderRef` to manage the recording process, with \'audio/webm\' format.\n\n\n**Implementing MediaRecorder Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `MediaRecorder` implementation. I\'m handling potential browser incompatibilities by implementing a fallback for unsupported formats. I\'m now integrating the `ondataavailable` event handler to collect audio chunks, and defining the `onstop` function to handle audio blob creation, base64 conversion, and submission through `submitJournal`. I\'ve also added the logic to stop tracks and remove the microphone icon.\n\n\n**Enhancing Audio Processing**\n\nI\'m now diving into the nitty-gritty of audio visualization. I\'ve integrated Web Audio API for real-time volume analysis, using `createMediaStreamSource` and `createAnalyser`. I\'m calculating an average volume from frequency data, updating the `micVolume` state. I\'m also ensuring efficient resource management with `animationFrameRef` for smooth updates, and implementing track stopping to conclude recording.\n\n\n**Finalizing Audio Control**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `stopRecording` function, ensuring a clean shutdown of all audio processes. I\'m focusing on handling the `MediaRecorder` instance by stopping it and clearing the `animationFrameRef`, and clearing the audio context to avoid memory leaks and ensure the app behaves responsively. I\'m also ensuring that visualizers stop when the recording is stopped.\n\n\n**Defining Submit Helper**\n\nI\'ve defined `submitJournal`, the central function for sending journal entries. It handles text and audio submissions, using `fetch` to POST to `/api/analyze-journal`. I\'m managing states such as `isSubmitting` and handling responses. I also implemented error handling and state updates after processing, to reset and update appropriately. I\'m taking care of potential crisis triggers too.\n\n\n**Adding Clinician Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating clinician-specific actions. I\'ve implemented `fetchHistory` to retrieve triage history data, triggered on tab changes. I\'ve also implemented `acknowledgeCrisis` which uses a POST to handle crisis acknowledgment, re-fetching history upon success. I\'m also preparing a \"clear history\" implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Clear History**\n\nI\'ve just added the `clearHistory` function. This uses a `DELETE` request to `/api/clear-history`. Upon a successful response, it triggers a `fetchHistory` update and clears any patient response bubbles. Error handling is also integrated to handle potential failures.\n\n\n**Designing Clinician Interface**\n\nI\'m now designing the clinician dashboard. I\'m focusing on key elements like analytics cards for summary metrics, controls for filtering, and an assessments grid to render patient records. I\'m implementing visual indicators like color-coded risk level badges and an escalation alert panel for crisis cases. I\'m also adding interactive buttons to manage patient interactions.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now write the full implementation of `/src/App.tsx` containing the Patient View, Clinician Dashboard, full browser-based audio recorder with actual mic visualizer feedback, crisis lockdown safety modals, in-memory sync queries, history management, and custom filter utilities. This implementation is modular, elegant, and uses standard, non-deprecated libraries."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 207073921
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
