    thinking: "**Updating the UI Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on updating `/src/App.tsx` to align with the Editorial Aesthetic design. This includes implementing the specified colors and fonts. Specifically, I\'m working on the main layout container\'s background, aiming for `bg-[#F8F9FA]` to kick things off.\n\n\n**Refining the Aesthetic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI elements. I\'m swapping out the hardcoded text color and updating the branding for the MindPortal AI Triage title. The switch buttons are styled, incorporating a soft border and subtle shadows for the selected state, and I\'m currently working on a toggle pill to improve functionality. I\'m focusing on creating an editorial and personalized welcome screen.\n\n\n**Personalizing the Welcome**\n\nI\'m now personalizing the welcome message. I\'ve decided to dynamically tailor the greeting, displaying either a personalized name like \"Sarah\" if available from the user\'s email or using a general welcome like \"Good day, friend\" as a default. The plan is to beautifully render this as a dynamic, editorial header using a specific font and color, aiming for an engaging user experience. I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s both welcoming and aligned with the intended aesthetic.\n\n\n\n**Designing the Recorder**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the recorder component. I\'m aiming for a visually appealing and intuitive interface. I\'m implementing a blue circle wrapper with a subtle shadow and centered text, using specific colors and fonts for different states (idle vs. recording). The goal is to make it look great and work even better. The validation response bubble will need a container to provide feedback.\n\n\n**Implementing the Validation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the validation response bubble and designing the crisis overlay. I\'ve styled the bubble with a light background, padding, rounded corners, and a border, adding a header and italicized text. The crisis overlay will be a full-screen, strictly-loc