steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1780048426
      nanos: 772606241
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Below is a prompt I generated using Gemini. Use whatever you can salvage from it to create a PWA and Gemma as the brain of ops. Tell me how it works once you\'ve implemented this. Deploy on Firebase by creating a project named \"SwaraSaathi\". Change the name mindportal and change its references to SwaraSaathi.\n\nI have already built the UI scaffold for a mobile-first Progressive Web App (PWA). I need the JavaScript logic and Node.js backend code to handle native audio processing and the Gemma 4 API integration. Please generate the code for the following three tasks:\n\nTask 1: Client-Side Acoustic Pre-Processing (Vanilla JS)\nWrite the JavaScript to capture microphone input using navigator.mediaDevices. Crucially, use the AudioContext API to downsample the stream strictly to 16,000 Hz and down-mix it to 1 channel (Mono) to match Gemma 4\'s acoustic requirements. Capture the 32-bit float data, convert it into a standard 16-bit PCM WAV Blob, and then encode that Blob into a Base64 string to be sent to the backend.\n\nTask 2: Gemma 4 Backend Payload (Node.js/Firebase Function)\nWrite a backend endpoint using the @google/genai SDK. It will receive the Base64 audio string.\n\nSet the model to gemma-4-e4b-it.\n\nPass the audio inline as audio/wav.\n\nWrite the System Instruction telling the model it is a dual-role clinical triage engine.\n\nForce a strict JSON response schema (responseSchema) containing exactly: patient_response (string), clinician_summary (object containing: primary_stressor, risk_level, clinical_notes, transcript), and crisis_trigger (boolean). Instruct the model to set crisis_trigger to true ONLY if there is an immediate risk of self-harm.\n\nTask 3: PWA Boilerplate\nProvide a minimal manifest.json, a basic offline-caching sw.js (Service Worker), and the brief JavaScript snippet needed in my main file to register the Service Worker so the app is installable on mobile.\""
    items {
      text: "Below is a prompt I generated using Gemini. Use whatever you can salvage from it to create a PWA and Gemma as the brain of ops. Tell me how it works once you\'ve implemented this. Deploy on Firebase by creating a project named \"SwaraSaathi\". Change the name mindportal and change its references to SwaraSaathi.\n\nI have already built the UI scaffold for a mobile-first Progressive Web App (PWA). I need the JavaScript logic and Node.js backend code to handle native audio processing and the Gemma 4 API integration. Please generate the code for the following three tasks:\n\nTask 1: Client-Side Acoustic Pre-Processing (Vanilla JS)\nWrite the JavaScript to capture microphone input using navigator.mediaDevices. Crucially, use the AudioContext API to downsample the stream strictly to 16,000 Hz and down-mix it to 1 channel (Mono) to match Gemma 4\'s acoustic requirements. Capture the 32-bit float data, convert it into a standard 16-bit PCM WAV Blob, and then encode that Blob into a Base64 string to be sent to the backend.\n\nTask 2: Gemma 4 Backend Payload (Node.js/Firebase Function)\nWrite a backend endpoint using the @google/genai SDK. It will receive the Base64 audio string.\n\nSet the model to gemma-4-e4b-it.\n\nPass the audio inline as audio/wav.\n\nWrite the System Instruction telling the model it is a dual-role clinical triage engine.\n\nForce a strict JSON response schema (responseSchema) containing exactly: patient_response (string), clinician_summary (object containing: primary_stressor, risk_level, clinical_notes, transcript), and crisis_trigger (boolean). Instruct the model to set crisis_trigger to true ONLY if there is an immediate risk of self-harm.\n\nTask 3: PWA Boilerplate\nProvide a minimal manifest.json, a basic offline-caching sw.js (Service Worker), and the brief JavaScript snippet needed in my main file to register the Service Worker so the app is installable on mobile.\""
    }
  }
}
