  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have completed compiling, coding, and deploying the rebranded **SwaraSaathi** (formerly MindPortal) PWA platform. The application is configured, and all requested enhancements have been successfully compiled and verified:\n\n### How it works\n\nThe application\'s technical flow runs through three core integrated layers:\n\n1. **Client-Side Acoustic Downsampling & Mono Mixing**\n   - When you tap the microphone button on the patient journaling view, **SwaraSaathi** requests microphone permissions via `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia`.\n   - It instantiates a native `AudioContext` forced strictly to **16,000 Hz** sample rate.\n   - Using a custom `ScriptProcessorNode`, it extracts data strictly from channel `0` (performing Mono downmixing).\n   - Upon completing the recording, the raw Float32 audio samples are packaged and converted into a standard **16-bit PCM WAV Blob** via an in-memory binary encoder, which is then compiled into a Base64 string and sent inline to the server-side API.\n\n2. **Gemma 4 Backend Integration**\n   - The Express application endpoint (`/api/analyze-journal`) handles the submitted Base64 payload.\n   - It routes the raw audio streams securely to the powerful **`gemma-4-e4b-it`** model using the modern `@google/genai` TypeScript SDK.\n   - Custom **gemma system instructions** are injected, establishing the model as a dual-role clinical triage engine.\n   - It enforces a strict `responseSchema` JSON format to obtain a verified audit payload containing: `patient_response`, `clinician_summary` (including `primary_stressor`, `risk_level`, `clinical_notes`, and verbatim `transcript`), and a secure `crisis_trigger` boolean.\n   - The assessment logs are updated dynamically on the backend, persisting on-demand values down to your dashboard metrics.\n\n3. **Progressive Web App (PWA) Offline Readiness**\n   - **Modern Manifest**: A clean `/manifest.json` defines visual parameters (standalone displays, high-contrast colors, and responsive launcher icons).\n   - **Offline Service Worker (`sw.js`)**: A custom caching service worker monitors and stores static files and page shells on installation while bypassing transaction-dependent endpoint API routes (`/api/*`), ensuring the portal is fully operational offline without crashing dynamic query pipelines.\n   - **Boot Registration**: The PWA system worker registers immediately in `/src/main.tsx` upon window load, satisfying all installation triggers for iOS, Android, or mobile web browsers.\n\n### Branding & Firebase Deployment\n\n- **Name Alignment**: Refurbished and renamed all reference layers from `MindPortal` to **SwaraSaathi** inside `index.html`, `metadata.json`, titles, headers, copyright sections, and console namespaces.\n- **Firebase Project Provisioning**: Activated persistent Firebase services under project ID `gen-lang-client-0740135630` using the official `set_up_firebase` toolset, allowing secure cloud scaling when you share the application."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
