  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Initial Approach**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user\'s questions, aiming for a beautifully crafted response. I\'m focusing on providing precise answers to each query. Right now, I\'m specifically tackling the API question, aiming for clarity.\n\n\n**Confirming Key Security**\n\nI\'ve confirmed our secure API key setup; the server securely handles the Google AI Studio key (`process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`), using `@google/genai` to connect to the Google GenAI Gateway. The keys remain hidden from the client. Next, I am clarifying that we can\'t provision Vertex AI directly; our environment lacks direct Google Cloud Console access. However, I\'ve confirmed Gemma 4 (`gemma-4-e4b-it`) is the underlying model!\n\n\n**Detailing Implemented Features**\n\nI\'ve successfully implemented all core functionalities! Gemma 4 is now used for generating transcripts, summarizing clinical observations, and classifying patient risk levels. Furthermore, a clinical score ranging from 1 to 100 has been added to augment both the backend schema and frontend Clinician tab, representing distress/clinical severity. This is uniquely displayed for medical practitioners.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully designed and integrated the clinician score and fully updated the application. Here is exactly how the system is wired, how we use the API, and how your tasks are executed:\n\n### \360\237\214\220 1. Google AI Studio API & Vertex AI Integration\n\n* **The API Key**: The application securely utilizes the **Google AI Studio API Key** (`process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`) on our custom backend server. Because key security is paramount, all model interaction is handled **server-side** (`/api/analyze-journal`), making sure no credentials or sensitive payloads are leaked to the client browser.\n* **Vertex AI vs. AI Studio**: In this environment, we operate in a sandboxed developer workspace and do not have administrative GCP IAM credentials to provision resources directly into your external Google Cloud Project on your behalf. However, we have **fully enabled Gemma 4** (configured with the correct `gemma-4-e4b-it` identifier) as the underlying engine using the modern `@google/genai` SDK inside our operational backend! \n\n---\n\n### \360\237\216\231\357\270\217 2. Audio Processing Flow (Self-Guided Diagnostic)\n\nFor every audio journal submitted, the application executes the following synchronized processing chain:\n\n1. **Client-Side Acoustic Pre-Processing**:\n   * Uses `navigator.mediaDevices` to capture raw user voice streams.\n   * Leverages the `AudioContext` API to instantiate a 16,000 Hz processing pipeline.\n   * Down-mixes the sound to a high-quality **1-channel (Mono) standard**.\n   * Converts the raw Float32 audio samples into a standard **16-bit PCM WAV Blob** on the fly, encodes it to **Base64**, and sends the inline payload safely to the backend.\n2. **Gemma 4 Triage Engine Processing**:\n   * **Generate a transcript**: Transcribes the raw acoustic audio verbatim into `transcript`.\n   * **Summarize**: Synthesizes a structured clinical summary with key therapeutic indicators inside `clinical_notes`.\n   * **Classify**: Assigns a direct diagnostic label representing the dominant psychological trigger under `primary_stressor`, determines the general `risk_level` (`Low`, `Medium`, or `High`), and flags an active `crisis_trigger` if life safety risk is detected.\n   * **Confidential Clinical Score**: Assigns a precise numerical distress rating from **1 (calm/baseline)** to **100 (critical active distress)** based on vocal content analysis.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\251\272 3. Clinician Distress Score Display (Hidden from Patients)\n\n* **Patient Dashboard (Empathetic View)**: The patient view focus remains strictly calming and therapeutic. Patients can only see warm, reassuring peer validation responses and self-guided health tips.\n* **Clinician Triage Panel (Confiential Diagnostic View)**:\n  * When practitioners switch to the clinician tab, they are met with a dedicated case queue displaying the dynamic transcripts, stressors, clinical logs, and the new **Confidential Severity Meter**.\n  * The **Clinical Triage Score** is visualized through an elegant horizontal progress bar that transitions from **emerald green** (low strain) to **amber/orange** (medium distress) to **deep crimson red** (active risk) with clear status metrics.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\223\261 4. PWA Core Implementation & Project Branding\n\n* All occurrences of `mindportal` have been fully upgraded and renamed to **SwaraSaathi**.\n* **PWA Features Installed**:\n  * `/public/manifest.json` defines your mobile identity with high-contrast launcher icons, dark system themes (`#1A1A1A`), and vertical display standalones.\n  * `/public/sw.js` registers a robust offline service worker to cache critical layouts with safe network fallbacks.\n  * `/src/main.tsx` automatically registers the Service Worker on boot.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 135400685
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
