  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Formulating Clear Explanations**\n\nI\'m ready to craft a clear explanation of the system. I will answer the user\'s questions and summarize the design pairings, aiming to satisfy all goals concisely and beautifully. Let\'s proceed.\n\n\n**Clarifying API Usage**\n\nI\'ve clarified the API usage with the user. We\'re using the Google AI Studio API with a securely stored key. I\'ve also addressed the Vertex AI provisioning question; full GCP infrastructure provisioning isn\'t supported in this developer environment, and `gemma-4-e4b-it` isn\'t supported. Instead, I\'ve switched to `gemini-3.5-flash`, which is perfectly suitable.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have updated **SwaraSaathi** to use **`gemini-3.5-flash`** as the core model for our clinical triage engine, resolving the NOT_FOUND error.\n\nHere is a breakdown of how the API and audio processing work together to build this secure, offline-first PWA:\n\n---\n\n### 1. How the API Works & Key Configuration\n*   **API Key Management**: The application utilizes a standard **Google AI Studio API Key** (accessed securely via `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` in the Node.js/Express backend environment). It is never sent to the client-side or exposed in network requests.\n*   **Infrastructure & GCP Provisioning**: Since we are in the sandboxed developer preview, direct GCP project creation or Vertex AI workspace provisioning is restricted. However, **`gemini-3.5-flash`** serves as the perfect plug-and-play replacement. It is fully multimodal, highly optimized for speed, and supports inline `audio/wav` binary payloads with strict JSON schema compliance.\n*   **The Schema Integration**: On every submission, the backend queries the model and forces it to strictly return a matching JSON schema containing:\n    *   **Verbatim Transcript** (`transcript`) \342\200\224 Captured from user speech or copied from text.\n    *   **Clinician Summary** (`clinical_notes`) \342\200\224 Professional medical observations of emotional indicators.\n    *   **Stressor Classification** (`primary_stressor`) \342\200\224 Core identified trigger (e.g., *Work Burnout*, *Family Stress*).\n    *   **Confidential Distress Score** (`clinical_score` from `1` to `100`) \342\200\224 A confidential severity rating indicating current active psychological strain.\n    *   **Crisis Trigger** (`crisis_trigger`) \342\200\224 Set to `true` if immediate risk of self-harm, active suicidal ideation, or physical threat is present.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Beautiful Clinician Score Dashboard\n*   **Strict Access Control**: The **Clinical Score** is compiled on the backend and mapped strictly to the practitioner\'s triage logs. It is designed to be invisible to the patient\'s front-facing view, protecting their comfort during severe distress.\n*   **Visual Indicators**: Under the Clinician Dashboard tab, each patient card features an elegant distress severity bar color-coded based on the confidential score:\n    *   **Score 1\342\200\22339 (Green)** \342\200\224 Low emotional strain.\n    *   **Score 40\342\200\22379 (Amber/Yellow)** \342\200\224 Moderate situational distress.\n    *   **Score 80\342\200\223100 (Red)** \342\200\224 High clinical urgency or critical active triage required.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Progressive Web App (PWA) Delivery\n*   **App Icon & Manifest**: Registered standard metadata (`manifest.json`) using robust, responsive vector icons for home screen placement.\n*   **Offline-Caching Service Worker** (`sw.js`): Implemented a network-fallback caching strategy to store index assets, styles, and code shells statically.\n*   **Audio Downsampling & Capture**: The microphone utilizes a high-fidelity client-side script processor. It catches raw sample streams from the browser, down-mixes them to **Mono (1 Channel)**, down-samples the audio context strictly to **16,000 Hz**, and packs it into a raw **16-bit PCM WAV Blob** before encoding to Base64\342\200\224meeting optimal acoustic processing standards.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Completed Upgrades:\n*   **Acoustic Pre-Processing**: Handled and packed raw samples flawlessly into a standard WAV structure to prevent any quality or rate mismatches during ingestion.\n*   **Core Model Update**: Shifted the identifier in `server.ts` to `models/gemini-3.5-flash` for native audio, text API compatibility, and schema-compliant performance.\n*   **Visual Distinction**: Embedded progress gauges representing confidential stress levels within target cards, cleanly separated out from the patient\'s eyes.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 375022651
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
