    summary: "To enable Gemma deployment on Vertex AI in Google Cloud, you need to complete several setup steps and then follow a deployment process, primarily through Vertex AI Model Garden or programmatically.\n\nHere\'s a breakdown of the steps:\n\n**1. Google Cloud Project Setup and API Activation**\nBefore deploying Gemma, ensure your Google Cloud environment is properly configured:\n*   **Create or Select a Google Cloud Project:** You must have an active Google Cloud project. If you\'re new to Google Cloud, you can create an account and receive free credits.[1]\n*   **Enable Billing:** Billing must be enabled for your Google Cloud project.[1]\n*   **Enable Vertex AI API:** The Vertex AI API needs to be enabled within your selected Google Cloud project. This can be done through the Google Cloud console.[1][2][3]\n\n**2. Local Machine Setup (for programmatic deployment)**\nFor deploying Gemma programmatically, you\'ll need to set up your local environment:\n*   **Install and Initialize Google Cloud CLI:** Install the Google Cloud Command Line Interface (CLI) on your local machine. If already installed, ensure your `gcloud` components are updated by running `gcloud components update`. Authenticate the gcloud CLI by generating Application Default Credentials (ADC) with `gcloud auth application-default login`.[1][2][3]\n*   **Install Vertex AI SDK:** Install the Vertex AI SDK for your preferred programming language, such as Python, using `pip3 install --upgrade \"google-cloud-aiplatform>=1.64\"`. You may also need to install the Protocol Buffers library: `pip3 install --upgrade \"protobuf>=5.28\"`.[1][2]\n\n**3. Deploying Gemma on Vertex AI**\n\nThere are a few primary methods for deploying Gemma models on Vertex AI:\n\n*   **Using Vertex AI Model Garden (Recommended for ease of use):**\n    1.  Navigate to the **Model Garden** page in the Google Cloud console.[4][2]\n    2.  Browse and select the specific Gemma model card you wish to deploy (e.g., Gemma 3 1B, Gemma 2 2B).[1][2]\n    3.  Click the \"Deploy\" button. In the deployment pane, choose \"Vertex AI\" as your deployment environment.[2]\n    4.  Follow the prompts to configure and deploy the model directly from the console.[4]\n\n*   **Programmatic Deployment (using Vertex AI SDK or gcloud CLI):**\n    1.  **Provision a Dedicated Endpoint:** Create a dedicated endpoint for your Gemma model using the Vertex AI SDK\'s `aiplatform.Endpoint.create()` method. This ensures a scalable and managed environment for model hosting.[5][3][6]\n    2.  **Register the Model:** Upload and register the Gemma model within the Vertex AI Model Registry. This involves specifying the serving container image (such as the Vertex AI Model Garden vLLM pre-built Docker image), environment variables, and serving arguments to optimize performance (e.g., `--gpu-memory-utilization`, `--max-model-len`).[5][3][6]\n    3.  **Deploy to the Endpoint:** Deploy the registered model to the dedicated endpoint you provisioned earlier.[5][3][6]\n    You can also use the `gcloud ai model-garden models deploy` command for programmatic deployment.[1]\n\n*   **Deploying on Cloud Run:**\n    Gemma models can also be deployed to Cloud Run, often utilizing pre-built containers that leverage Ollama for serving or vLLM for efficient inference.[4][7][8] Google AI Studio offers a streamlined, one-click deployment process for Gemma to Cloud Run. This typically involves selecting a Gemma model in Google AI Studio, choosing \"Deploy to Cloud Run,\" and following the prompts to create or select a Google Cloud project.[9]\n\n**Key Considerations for Deployment:**\n*   **vLLM:** For fast and efficient serving of Gemma models, especially on GPU-backed endpoints, vLLM is frequently utilized. It provides features like PagedAttention, continuous batching, and optimized CUDA kernels.[5][8]\n*   **Machine and Accelerator Types:** You can view the supported machine types, accelerator types, and container image URIs for a specific model using the `gcloud ai model-garden models list-deployment-config` command.[1]\n*   **Fine-tuning:** If you intend to fine-tune Gemma, Vertex AI supports this using techniques like PEFT (LoRA) from Hugging Face.[5] Ray on Vertex AI is another platform that can be used for fine-tuning.[10]\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGddXGnff_bPWvXmI8_JRaCFMFTd4s4e9P8Khg659iAiT0u8Zwj1RYpcSErNXDqNolj9pXG5gpY8zCzcw3IaJe5qpqdq4k-I1lTdqw-kgHqucN9xDHhaw-wpVqidNrxHW1pHRADXi39sHvJB_RsHVOMYVJyD6wam7fMd-nmXIv117P4-5MDJz47XGOVpaYTNLgDGFt3TaxFAlzCFNSSI_0H)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH9muASdhapDfRb3EMa9TTDl-NgQfQNZLpRPwtRCOWvOIAzz2iv6-ldx-eP5GzG23YwoBYlrxnTr4kj2n928ixAv4pCzziJgR5Fh9rb2BPqaNjL6mUuBjvXXMPGUMPyDBMvC32hmga0qT0ExWBwrm919J5u58l-sLbSP5SVQaa19ZJ_69pAx4v3ywXW9OLB2a3xGjh1swFgyiTmSFdSzTOfQwVZeg==)\n[3] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFV2V43IXpBvLY2KEVV0f3aM-EkA_gBAlo1rSzIvLfJZEJAWUTai2ykm5tmOhsO44SenY_DXNWUvZtDXsiWR7fL4JwNpLHgRRqVvq1ayoTYWS5De24ThvA-gUorDSt22OVhpWlYOtP44hK3geCh0WxBufEIw1quMKDf4UJBnh_nVcVR8wqUgzySHTOnDHrf8W8pTpLZM-JQr5jl)\n[4] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQELeUucemkv2cq7ps7c7XE9DvLc6BaXKeLz1Suv89AP0GuKte3kSJvzvJn1F9oqJkFUO7EMph4qRuFCbxVSg43jS3naiQ2UNI_e-FlPs5CF_W5ftefzzn9zcnnI8V7HEpt4sCQT-C-HIt6i7wyHHmNfO41w9tE=)\n[5] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF8hMzcXoE-Sp2Ehtjla7fFuUXr3QluOJLQJwewSMBrwtY2z-LK7t2BLEjmY4JJDGq5AC2Znb3gfeu1h7ITF7J-HSOvGsQMzSXWoQIY1j5ctivWVIE0MJvoYoZ_1qoEpgGgsRPdMINkm9zwD2VzINI4kSLuh6jyhm5rLKVrfhGUzFh7FYMcUHrTOgACK_y24QwtTOjLpTc=)\n[6] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHyzVmjPe8tfGQP5oIl4qKGr4pvLBEAe-RKBHLSZLYiwqg1eL6gGS7cYyscnDv8AwmWPYDLAfcTyx3tXqyxf6xX7-4bRTSQRBp9JW07Ku2iO0BTi7y-vGuWig7vEsCGa8fsDBIawpot8qaMtZu7bzA2wPkR1e3Ut